⍝ lib/numtheory.imo — spec notation — trusted prelude, part 15: number theory over ℤ and ℤ[i]
⍝ Every algorithm works on the base i−1 digit strings (𝔇) of the integers involved, with the digit operations of parts 2 and 6
⍝ (⊞ᶻ ⊟ᶻ ⊠ᶻ ⫽ᶻ ⋚ʳ …).  Facts of the base that are used throughout (b = i − 1):
⍝   * b⁴ = −4 and b⁸ = 16, so dropping 4 digits of a multiple of 4 divides it by −4: base 4 is native, up to a sign;
⍝   * a real integer has digit d₁ = 0 and d₂ = d₃, so  n mod 2 = d₀,  n mod 4 = d₀ + 2d₃,  n mod 8 = d₀ + 2d₃ + 4(d₄ ⊻ d₅);
⍝   * (1 + i) divides z exactly when its last digit is 0, and z / b is z without that digit: the prime above 2 is the base.
⍝ ---- conversions, comparisons, small helpers on real integers
up_nt ∶ 𝔇 → ℚ[i]
up_nt ξ ≔ (⊗ (⊡ ξ) (◀ 1))
⍝ equality of two Gaussian integers, whatever their trailing zero digits (⊞ᶻ ⊟ᶻ ⊠ᶻ do not remove them, so ≡ is not enough)
eqz_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔹
eqz_nt ξ η ≔ (∅ᶻ (⊟ᶻ ξ η))
lt_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔹
lt_nt ξ η ≔ ((⋚ʳ (⊟ᶻ ξ η)) ⊤ ⊥ ⊥)
⍝ ξ mod ν for a real ξ of any sign and a natural ν  (ξ mod 0 = ξ)
mod_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇
mod_nt ξ ν ≔ ((∅ᶻ ν) ξ ((⋚ʳ ξ) ((ρ ↦ ((∅ᶻ ρ) ⊥ (⊟ᶻ ν ρ))) (▶ (⫽ᶻ (⊖ᶻ ξ) ν))) ⊥ (▶ (⫽ᶻ ξ ν))))
⍝ ⌊ξ / ν⌋ for naturals (ν > 0)
dv_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇
dv_nt ξ ν ≔ (◀ (⫽ᶻ ξ ν))
⍝ sgn(θ)·ξ
sg_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇
sg_nt θ ξ ≔ ((⋚ʳ θ) (⊖ᶻ ξ) ⊥ ξ)
⍝ ---- the 2-adic part.  While the last digit of an even value is 0, the last two digits are 0 and dropping them divides by b² = −2i;
⍝ after k drops the value is (ξ / 2ᵏ)·iᵏ, and a unit fixes it.  v2_nt ξ = (k as a unary list, the odd part of ξ)   (ξ ≠ 0)
v2′_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔓 (𝔏 𝔹) 𝔇
v2′_nt ξ υ ≔ ((⌃ ξ) (⊗ υ ξ) (v2′_nt (⌄ (⌄ ξ)) (∷ ⊤ υ)))
⍝ ξ·(−i)ᵏ, with k mod 4 counted in two bits ϑ ϖ while the unary list is walked
um_nt ∶ 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔹 → 𝔹 → 𝔇 → 𝔇
um_nt υ ϑ ϖ ξ ≔ (υ (σ τ ↦ (um_nt τ (¬ ϑ) (⊻ ϖ ϑ) ξ)) (ϑ (ϖ (⊞ᶻ ξ (𝕓 ξ)) (⊖ᶻ (⊞ᶻ ξ (𝕓 ξ)))) (ϖ (⊖ᶻ ξ) ξ)))
v2_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔓 (𝔏 𝔹) 𝔇
v2_nt ξ ≔ ((θ ↦ (⊗ (◀ θ) (um_nt (◀ θ) ⊥ ⊥ (▶ θ)))) (v2′_nt ξ ⊥))
⍝ the binary digits of a natural number, least significant first
bits_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔏 𝔹
bits_nt ξ ≔ ((∅ᶻ ξ) ⊥ (∷ (⌃ ξ) (bits_nt (⌊½⌋ᶻ ξ))))
⍝ ---- Montgomery arithmetic modulo an odd N > 0, in base 4.  A residue x is held as any real x̃ ≡ x·R (mod N), |x̃| < 2N, where
⍝ R = (b⁴)ᵐ = (−4)ᵐ, m = ⌈L/4⌉ + 3 for N of L digits (N < 2.42·2^(L/2), so 4ᵐ > 26·N).  Reduction (REDC) divides by b⁴ m times:
⍝ T ≡ t (mod 4) is read off the digits (t = d₀ + 2d₃), the multiple c·N with T + c·N ≡ 0 (mod 4) is added (c ∈ {0,1,2,3}, N⁻¹ ≡ N
⍝ mod 4), and the four zero digits are dropped — no division and no comparison.  |T| < 26N² gives |REDC T| < N + |T|/4ᵐ < 2N.
⍝ mlt_nt N = (c·N for t = 1, (2N, c·N for t = 3))
mlt_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔓 𝔇 (𝔓 𝔇 𝔇)
mlt_nt ν ≔ ((θ ι ↦ ((⌃ (⌄ (⌄ (⌄ ν)))) (⊗ ν (⊗ θ ι)) (⊗ ι (⊗ θ ν)))) (⊞ᶻ ν ν) (⊞ᶻ ν (⊞ᶻ ν ν)))
stp_nt ∶ 𝔓 𝔇 (𝔓 𝔇 𝔇) → 𝔇 → 𝔇
stp_nt μ τ ≔ (⌄⁴ ((⌃ τ) ((⌃ (⌄ (⌄ (⌄ τ)))) (⊞ᶻ τ (▶ (▶ μ))) (⊞ᶻ τ (◀ μ))) ((⌃ (⌄ (⌄ (⌄ τ)))) (⊞ᶻ τ (◀ (▶ μ))) τ)))
⍝ REDC: one step per block of four digits of the counter ν (the digits of N), and three more
rdc_nt ∶ 𝔓 𝔇 (𝔓 𝔇 𝔇) → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇
rdc_nt μ ν τ ≔ ((∅ ν) (stp_nt μ (stp_nt μ (stp_nt μ τ))) (rdc_nt μ (⌄⁴ ν) (stp_nt μ τ)))
⍝ R² = b⁸ᵐ = 16ᵐ: eight zero digits per step, then 1
pw_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇
pw_nt ν ≔ ((∅ ν) (𝕓⁴ (𝕓⁴ (𝕓⁴ (𝕓⁴ (𝕓⁴ (𝕓⁴ (◀ 1))))))) (𝕓⁴ (𝕓⁴ (pw_nt (⌄⁴ ν)))))
⍝ the representative in [0, N) of a value within a few N of it
nrm_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇
nrm_nt ν ξ ≔ ((⋚ʳ ξ) (nrm_nt ν (⊞ᶻ ξ ν)) ⊥ ((⩾ᶻ ξ ν) (nrm_nt ν (⊟ᶻ ξ ν)) ξ))
⍝ ---- a modular context  K = (mul, (enc, (dec, (one, (nrm, N)))))  for a natural modulus N:  mul multiplies representatives, enc maps
⍝ x ∈ [0, N) to its representative, dec maps a representative back to [0, N), one represents 1, nrm makes a representative canonical
⍝ (equal residues ⇔ equal canonical representatives).  Odd N: Montgomery;  even N: products reduced by long division (⫽ᶻ);
⍝ N = 0: plain arithmetic in ℤ.
mctx_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔓 (𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇) (𝔓 (𝔇 → 𝔇) (𝔓 (𝔇 → 𝔇) (𝔓 𝔇 (𝔓 (𝔇 → 𝔇) 𝔇))))
mctx_nt ν ≔ ((μ ↦ ((ρ ↦ (⊗ (ξ η ↦ (rdc_nt μ ν (⊠ᶻ ξ η))) (⊗ (ξ ↦ (rdc_nt μ ν (⊠ᶻ ξ ρ))) (⊗ (ξ ↦ (nrm_nt ν (rdc_nt μ ν ξ))) (⊗ (rdc_nt μ ν ρ) (⊗ (nrm_nt ν) ν)))))) (▶ (⫽ᶻ (pw_nt ν) ν)))) (mlt_nt ν))
pctx_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔓 (𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇) (𝔓 (𝔇 → 𝔇) (𝔓 (𝔇 → 𝔇) (𝔓 𝔇 (𝔓 (𝔇 → 𝔇) 𝔇))))
pctx_nt ν ≔ (⊗ (ξ η ↦ (▶ (⫽ᶻ (⊠ᶻ ξ η) ν))) (⊗ (ξ ↦ ξ) (⊗ (ξ ↦ ξ) (⊗ (▶ (⫽ᶻ (◀ 1) ν)) (⊗ (ξ ↦ ξ) ν)))))
ctx_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔓 (𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇) (𝔓 (𝔇 → 𝔇) (𝔓 (𝔇 → 𝔇) (𝔓 𝔇 (𝔓 (𝔇 → 𝔇) 𝔇))))
ctx_nt ν ≔ ((∅ᶻ ν) (⊗ ⊠ᶻ (⊗ (ξ ↦ ξ) (⊗ (ξ ↦ ξ) (⊗ (◀ 1) (⊗ (ξ ↦ ξ) ⊥))))) ((⌃ ν) (mctx_nt ν) (pctx_nt ν)))
⍝ accessors
kmul_nt ∶ 𝔓 (𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇) (𝔓 (𝔇 → 𝔇) (𝔓 (𝔇 → 𝔇) (𝔓 𝔇 (𝔓 (𝔇 → 𝔇) 𝔇)))) → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇
kmul_nt κ ≔ (◀ κ)
kenc_nt ∶ 𝔓 (𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇) (𝔓 (𝔇 → 𝔇) (𝔓 (𝔇 → 𝔇) (𝔓 𝔇 (𝔓 (𝔇 → 𝔇) 𝔇)))) → 𝔇 → 𝔇
kenc_nt κ ≔ (◀ (▶ κ))
kdec_nt ∶ 𝔓 (𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇) (𝔓 (𝔇 → 𝔇) (𝔓 (𝔇 → 𝔇) (𝔓 𝔇 (𝔓 (𝔇 → 𝔇) 𝔇)))) → 𝔇 → 𝔇
kdec_nt κ ≔ (◀ (▶ (▶ κ)))
kone_nt ∶ 𝔓 (𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇) (𝔓 (𝔇 → 𝔇) (𝔓 (𝔇 → 𝔇) (𝔓 𝔇 (𝔓 (𝔇 → 𝔇) 𝔇)))) → 𝔇
kone_nt κ ≔ (◀ (▶ (▶ (▶ κ))))
knrm_nt ∶ 𝔓 (𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇) (𝔓 (𝔇 → 𝔇) (𝔓 (𝔇 → 𝔇) (𝔓 𝔇 (𝔓 (𝔇 → 𝔇) 𝔇)))) → 𝔇 → 𝔇
knrm_nt κ ≔ (◀ (▶ (▶ (▶ (▶ κ)))))
⍝ ξ^ε in a context: right-to-left square and multiply over the bits β of ε; the last square is never forced
kpw′_nt ∶ (𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇) → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔇
kpw′_nt μ ρ ξ β ≔ (β (σ τ ↦ (kpw′_nt μ (σ (μ ρ ξ) ρ) (μ ξ ξ) τ)) ρ)
kpw_nt ∶ 𝔓 (𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇) (𝔓 (𝔇 → 𝔇) (𝔓 (𝔇 → 𝔇) (𝔓 𝔇 (𝔓 (𝔇 → 𝔇) 𝔇)))) → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇
kpw_nt κ ξ ε ≔ (kpw′_nt (kmul_nt κ) (kone_nt κ) ξ (bits_nt ε))
⍝ θ^ε mod ν for θ ∈ [0, ν) (any θ when ν = 0) and ε ≥ 0
pmd_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇
pmd_nt ν θ ε ≔ ((κ ↦ (kdec_nt κ (kpw_nt κ (kenc_nt κ θ) ε))) (ctx_nt ν))
⍝ ---- extended Euclid.  On naturals with ⫽ᶻ; signs are put back afterwards.  On ℤ[i] with the nearest quotient quoᶻ (N(r) ≤ N(b)/2),
⍝ the gcd then normalised to Re > 0, Im ≥ 0 by the unit u = ⌜g⌝ / g, which also multiplies the cofactors.
eg_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔓 𝔇 (𝔓 𝔇 𝔇)
eg_nt ρ ρ′ σ σ′ τ τ′ ≔ ((∅ᶻ ρ′) (⊗ ρ (⊗ σ τ)) ((χ ↦ (eg_nt ρ′ (▶ χ) σ′ (⊟ᶻ σ (⊠ᶻ (◀ χ) σ′)) τ′ (⊟ᶻ τ (⊠ᶻ (◀ χ) τ′)))) (⫽ᶻ ρ ρ′)))
egz_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔓 𝔇 (𝔓 𝔇 𝔇)
egz_nt θ ι ≔ ((χ ↦ (⊗ (◀ χ) (⊗ (sg_nt θ (◀ (▶ χ))) (sg_nt ι (▶ (▶ χ)))))) (eg_nt (absᶻ θ) (absᶻ ι) (◀ 1) ⊥ ⊥ (◀ 1)))
egg_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔓 𝔇 (𝔓 𝔇 𝔇)
egg_nt ρ ρ′ σ σ′ τ τ′ ≔ ((∅ᶻ ρ′) (⊗ ρ (⊗ σ τ)) ((χ ↦ (egg_nt ρ′ (⊡ (⊟ᶻ ρ (⊠ᶻ χ ρ′))) σ′ (⊟ᶻ σ (⊠ᶻ χ σ′)) τ′ (⊟ᶻ τ (⊠ᶻ χ τ′)))) (quoᶻ ρ ρ′)))
egi_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔓 𝔇 (𝔓 𝔇 𝔇)
egi_nt θ ι ≔ ((χ ↦ ((υ ↦ (⊗ (⌜ᶻ (◀ χ)) (⊗ (⊠ᶻ υ (◀ (▶ χ))) (⊠ᶻ υ (▶ (▶ χ)))))) (÷ᶻ (⌜ᶻ (◀ χ)) (◀ χ)))) (egg_nt θ ι (◀ 1) ⊥ ⊥ (◀ 1)))
egcd ∶ ℤ → ℤ → 𝔓 ℕ (𝔓 ℤ ℤ)      ⍝ Bézout: (g, (s, t)) with s·a + t·b = g = gcd(a, b) ≥ 0 (extended Euclid; egcd(0, 0) = (0, (0, 0)))
egcd ∶ ℤ[i] → ℤ[i] → 𝔓 ℤ[i] (𝔓 ℤ[i] ℤ[i])
egcd ξ η ≔ ((θ ι ↦ ((χ ↦ (⊗ (up_nt (◀ χ)) (⊗ (up_nt (◀ (▶ χ))) (up_nt (▶ (▶ χ)))))) ((∧ (realᶻ θ) (realᶻ ι)) (egz_nt θ ι) (egi_nt θ ι)))) (↓ᶻ ξ) (↓ᶻ η))
⍝ ---- inverses and powers modulo n
minv_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇
minv_nt θ ν ≔ ((χ ↦ ((eqz_nt (◀ χ) (◀ 1)) (mod_nt (◀ (▶ χ)) ν) ⊥)) (egz_nt θ ν))
gminv_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇
gminv_nt θ ι ≔ ((χ ↦ ((eqz_nt (◀ χ) (◀ 1)) (remᶻ (◀ (▶ χ)) ι) ⊥)) (egi_nt θ ι))
modinv ∶ ℕ → ℕ → ℕ      ⍝ the inverse of a modulo n, in [0, n); 0 when gcd(a, n) ≠ 1 (modulo 0: a itself when a = ±1, else 0); on ℤ[i] reduced by rem (0 when not invertible)
modinv ∶ ℤ → ℕ → ℤ
modinv ∶ ℤ[i] → ℤ[i] → ℤ[i]
modinv ξ ζ ≔ ((θ ι ↦ (up_nt ((∧ (realᶻ θ) (realᶻ ι)) (minv_nt θ (absᶻ ι)) (gminv_nt θ ι)))) (↓ᶻ ξ) (↓ᶻ ζ))
powmod ∶ ℕ → ℤ → ℕ → ℕ      ⍝ aᵉ mod n in [0, n), square and multiply (Montgomery multiplication in base 4 = −(i−1)⁴ for odd n); e < 0 through modinv(a, n) (so 0 when a is not invertible); modulo 0 it is aᵉ in ℤ
powmod ∶ ℤ → ℤ → ℕ → ℤ
powmod ξ η ζ ≔ ((ν ε ↦ (up_nt ((⋚ʳ ε) (pmd_nt ν (mod_nt (↓ᶻ (modinv ξ ζ)) ν) (⊖ᶻ ε)) (pmd_nt ν (mod_nt (↓ᶻ ξ) ν) ε) (pmd_nt ν (mod_nt (↓ᶻ ξ) ν) ε)))) (↓ᶻ ζ) (↓ᶻ η))
⍝ ---- primality.  Below 42: the list of primes; below 43² = 1849: trial division by the primes to 41.  Above: one gcd with 2·3·5·…·41
⍝ removes every number with a small factor, and the strong (Miller–Rabin) test is made with the bases 2, 3, 5, …, 41 in turn:
⍝ after base number k the answer is certain as soon as n < ψₖ, the least composite that passes the first k bases (OEIS A014233;
⍝ ψ₁₃ = 3317044064679887385961981 ≈ 3.3·10²⁴).  Above ψ₁₃ every one of the 13 bases is tried, and a number passing them all must
⍝ also pass the strong Lucas test (lsp_nt): together the Baillie–PSW test, for which no composite that passes is known.
spr_nt ∶ 𝔏 𝔇
spr_nt ≔ (∷ (◀ 1100) (∷ (◀ 1101) (∷ (◀ 111010001) (∷ (◀ 111011101) (∷ (◀ 111001101) (∷ (◀ 100010001) (∷ (◀ 100000001) (∷ (◀ 100001101) (∷ (◀ 110011011101) (∷ (◀ 110000010001) (∷ (◀ 110000011101) (∷ (◀ 110111010001) (∷ (◀ 110111000001) ⊥)))))))))))))
mrb_nt ∶ 𝔏 (𝔓 𝔇 𝔇)
mrb_nt ≔ (∷ (⊗ (◀ 1100) (◀ 1110000000000000000011101)) (∷ (⊗ (◀ 1101) (◀ 11001101000100000000110111000001110011010001)) (∷ (⊗ (◀ 111010001) (◀ 1100110000000000110111011101000011001100110100000001)) (∷ (⊗ (◀ 111011101) (◀ 10001000000000000110011000000110011000000000111000001000111011101)) (∷ (⊗ (◀ 111001101) (◀ 110000000000110100010000110000000000110100000000000000011101000111011101000011001101)) (∷ (⊗ (◀ 100010001) (◀ 110100001101110000010000000111000000110100001100000000001100000100010001110000011101)) (∷ (⊗ (◀ 100000001) (◀ 1100110100001101110111001101110100001101000100001101110011010000110100010001110000010001000000000001)) (∷ (⊗ (◀ 100001101) (◀ 1100110100001101110111001101110100001101000100001101110011010000110100010001110000010001000000000001)) (∷ (⊗ (◀ 110011011101) (◀ 111010000110100010000110011011100110000010000000100001101110000001101000100000000110011001100110100000000110011000000000011001101)) (∷ (⊗ (◀ 110000010001) (◀ 111010000110100010000110011011100110000010000000100001101110000001101000100000000110011001100110100000000110011000000000011001101)) (∷ (⊗ (◀ 110000011101) (◀ 111010000110100010000110011011100110000010000000100001101110000001101000100000000110011001100110100000000110011000000000011001101)) (∷ (⊗ (◀ 110111010001) (◀ 11101000111010000110000001100110100011101110000010000110111000000000011001100000000000000110011000000000000010001110000011101110000010000110000000001110111010001)) (∷ (⊗ (◀ 110111000001) (◀ 11010001000000011101110111011100110011010001000011001100110100011100000100011101110011001101000011000000110111010000000000010000000111001101110111000000000000010001)) ⊥)))))))))))))
⍝ ---- the strong Lucas test (with Miller–Rabin it makes the Baillie–PSW test).  Selfridge's parameters: D the first of 5, −7, 9, −11, …
⍝ with (D/n) = −1 (0 when a D has a proper common factor with n), P = 1, Q = (1 − D)/4.  With n + 1 = d·2ˢ (d odd), n passes when
⍝ U_d ≡ 0 or V_(d·2ʳ) ≡ 0 for some r < s.  U, V and Qᵏ are Montgomery representatives (the products need no other reduction; the
⍝ linear combinations are reduced by mod): the doubling U₂ₖ = UₖVₖ, V₂ₖ = Vₖ² − 2Qᵏ, Q²ᵏ = (Qᵏ)², and for a bit 1 the step
⍝ Uₖ₊₁ = (Uₖ + Vₖ)/2, Vₖ₊₁ = (D·Uₖ + Vₖ)/2, Qᵏ⁺¹ = Qᵏ·Q, run over the bits of d after the leading one; x/2 mod n is x/2 or (x + n)/2.
sfd_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇
sfd_nt ν δ ≔ ((γ ↦ ((∧ (lt_nt (◀ 1) γ) (lt_nt γ ν)) ⊥ ((≐ (jac_nt (mod_nt δ ν) ν ⊥) 11101) δ (sfd_nt ν ((lt_nt ⊥ δ) (⊟ᶻ (⊖ᶻ δ) (◀ 1100)) (⊞ᶻ (⊖ᶻ δ) (◀ 1100))))))) (gcdᶻ δ ν))
hlf_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇
hlf_nt ν ξ ≔ (½ᶻ ((⌃ ξ) (⊞ᶻ ξ ν) ξ))
lst_nt ∶ 𝔓 (𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇) (𝔓 (𝔇 → 𝔇) (𝔓 (𝔇 → 𝔇) (𝔓 𝔇 (𝔓 (𝔇 → 𝔇) 𝔇)))) → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔓 𝔇 (𝔓 𝔇 𝔇) → 𝔹 → 𝔓 𝔇 (𝔓 𝔇 𝔇)
lst_nt κ ν δ χ ψ σ ≔ ((υ′ ϑ′ ϖ′ ↦ (σ (⊗ (hlf_nt ν (mod_nt (⊞ᶻ υ′ ϑ′) ν)) (⊗ (hlf_nt ν (mod_nt (⊞ᶻ (⊠ᶻ δ υ′) ϑ′) ν)) (mod_nt (⊠ᶻ χ ϖ′) ν))) (⊗ υ′ (⊗ ϑ′ ϖ′)))) (kmul_nt κ (◀ ψ) (◀ (▶ ψ))) (mod_nt (⊟ᶻ (kmul_nt κ (◀ (▶ ψ)) (◀ (▶ ψ))) (⊞ᶻ (▶ (▶ ψ)) (▶ (▶ ψ)))) ν) (kmul_nt κ (▶ (▶ ψ)) (▶ (▶ ψ))))
⍝ the remaining doublings of V (|υ| = s − 1 of them), looking for V ≡ 0
slr_nt ∶ 𝔓 (𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇) (𝔓 (𝔇 → 𝔇) (𝔓 (𝔇 → 𝔇) (𝔓 𝔇 (𝔓 (𝔇 → 𝔇) 𝔇)))) → 𝔇 → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔹
slr_nt κ ν υ ϑ ϖ ≔ (υ (σ τ ↦ ((ϑ′ ↦ ((∅ᶻ (knrm_nt κ ϑ′)) ⊤ (slr_nt κ ν τ ϑ′ (kmul_nt κ ϖ ϖ)))) (mod_nt (⊟ᶻ (kmul_nt κ ϑ ϑ) (⊞ᶻ ϖ ϖ)) ν))) ⊥)
⍝ the strong Lucas test of an odd ν > 1 with the parameter D
slq_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔹
