⍝ ---- discrete logarithm.  While g = gcd(a, n) > 1:  x = 0 if k ≡ b, else g | b is needed and k·aˣ ≡ b (mod n) becomes
⍝ (k·a/g)·aˣ⁻¹ ≡ b/g (mod n/g).  Then baby-step giant-step with s = ⌊√n⌋ + 1: the baby steps (b·a^q, q), q = 0 … s, and the giant
⍝ steps (k·a^(s·p), p), p = 1 … s, are sorted (merge sort, keeping the largest q and the least p of each value), and a merge of the two
⍝ lists gives every solution s·p − q of the least block; the least is the answer.
