⍝ (F(|n|), F(|n| + 1))
fbp_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔓 𝔇 𝔇
fbp_nt ν ≔ (fdb_nt (reverse (bits_nt (absᶻ ν))) (⊗ ⊥ (◀ 1)))
fib ∶ ℤ → ℤ      ⍝ the Fibonacci number F(n) (fast doubling); F(−n) = (−1)ⁿ⁺¹F(n)
fib ∶ ℕ → ℕ
fib ξ ≔ ((ν ↦ ((ψ ↦ (up_nt ((∧ (lt_nt ν ⊥) (¬ (⌃ ν))) (⊖ᶻ (◀ ψ)) (◀ ψ)))) (fbp_nt ν))) (↓ᶻ ξ))
lucas ∶ ℤ → ℤ      ⍝ the Lucas number L(n) = 2F(n+1) − F(n) (fast doubling); L(−n) = (−1)ⁿL(n)
lucas ∶ ℕ → ℕ
lucas ξ ≔ ((ν ↦ ((ψ ↦ ((ϑ ↦ (up_nt ((∧ (lt_nt ν ⊥) (⌃ ν)) (⊖ᶻ ϑ) ϑ))) (⊟ᶻ (⊞ᶻ (▶ ψ) (▶ ψ)) (◀ ψ)))) (fbp_nt ν))) (↓ᶻ ξ))
⍝ ---- combinatorial numbers
catalan ∶ ℕ → ℕ      ⍝ the Catalan number C(n) = (2n choose n)/(n + 1)
catalan ξ ≔ (up_nt (÷ᶻ (↓ᶻ (choose (⊞ ξ ξ) ξ)) (⊞ᶻ (↓ᶻ ξ) (◀ 1))))
⍝ a row of the Bell triangle from the previous one: it starts with the last element, each next is the previous plus the one above
bsc_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔏 𝔇 → 𝔏 𝔇
bsc_nt ξ ρ ≔ (∷ ξ (ρ (θ τ ↦ (bsc_nt (⊞ᶻ ξ θ) τ)) ⊥))
brw_nt ∶ 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 𝔇 → 𝔏 𝔇
brw_nt υ ρ ≔ (υ (σ τ ↦ (brw_nt τ (bsc_nt (last ρ) ρ))) ρ)
bell ∶ ℕ → ℕ      ⍝ the Bell number Bₙ (set partitions of n elements), by the Bell triangle: O(n²) additions
bell ξ ≔ (up_nt (hd (brw_nt (ud_nt (↓ᶻ ξ)) (∷ (◀ 1) ⊥))))
⍝ rows of Stirling numbers: S(n+1, j) = j·S(n, j) + S(n, j−1);  s(n+1, j) = s(n, j−1) − n·s(n, j)
ssr_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔏 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔏 𝔇
ssr_nt ι ρ π′ ≔ (ρ (θ τ ↦ (∷ (⊞ᶻ (⊠ᶻ ι θ) π′) (ssr_nt (⊞ᶻ ι (◀ 1)) τ θ))) (∷ π′ ⊥))
sfr_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔏 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔏 𝔇
sfr_nt ν ρ π′ ≔ (ρ (θ τ ↦ (∷ (⊟ᶻ π′ (⊠ᶻ ν θ)) (sfr_nt ν τ θ))) (∷ π′ ⊥))
ssl_nt ∶ 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 𝔇 → 𝔏 𝔇
ssl_nt υ ρ ≔ (υ (σ τ ↦ (ssl_nt τ (ssr_nt ⊥ ρ ⊥))) ρ)
sfl_nt ∶ 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔇 → 𝔏 𝔇 → 𝔏 𝔇
sfl_nt υ ν ρ ≔ (υ (σ τ ↦ (sfl_nt τ (⊞ᶻ ν (◀ 1)) (sfr_nt ν ρ ⊥))) ρ)
stirling₁ ∶ ℕ → ℕ → ℤ      ⍝ the signed Stirling number of the first kind s(n, k) (coefficient of xᵏ in x(x−1)…(x−n+1)), by rows: O(n·k)
stirling₁ ξ η ≔ (up_nt (hd (drop′ (↓ᶻ η) (sfl_nt (ud_nt (↓ᶻ ξ)) ⊥ (∷ (◀ 1) ⊥)))))
stirling₂ ∶ ℕ → ℕ → ℕ      ⍝ the Stirling number of the second kind S(n, k) (partitions of n elements into k blocks), by rows: O(n·k)
stirling₂ ξ η ≔ (up_nt (hd (drop′ (↓ᶻ η) (ssl_nt (ud_nt (↓ᶻ ξ)) (∷ (◀ 1) ⊥)))))
⍝ partitions: p(m) = Σₖ₌₁ (−1)ᵏ⁺¹ (p(m − k(3k−1)/2) + p(m − k(3k+1)/2)), read off the list ρ = p(m−1), p(m−2), …, p(0):
⍝ the generalised pentagonal numbers 1, 2, 5, 7, 12, 15, … are reached by dropping k − 1 … alternately k and 2k + 1 elements.
pps_nt ∶ 𝔏 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔹 → 𝔇
pps_nt ρ κ ς ≔ ((∅ ρ) ⊥ ((ρ′ ↦ ((ϑ ↦ ((ϖ ↦ (ς (⊞ᶻ ϑ ϖ) (⊟ᶻ ϖ ϑ))) (pps_nt (drop′ (⊞ᶻ (⊞ᶻ κ κ) (◀ 1)) ρ′) (⊞ᶻ κ (◀ 1)) (¬ ς)))) (⊞ᶻ (hd ρ) (hd ρ′)))) (drop′ κ ρ)))
ppl_nt ∶ 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 𝔇 → 𝔏 𝔇
ppl_nt υ ρ ≔ (υ (σ τ ↦ (ppl_nt τ (∷ (pps_nt ρ (◀ 1) ⊤) ρ))) ρ)
partitions ∶ ℕ → ℕ      ⍝ the partition number p(n), by Euler's pentagonal number recurrence: O(n^1.5) additions
partitions ξ ≔ (up_nt (hd (ppl_nt (ud_nt (↓ᶻ ξ)) (∷ (◀ 1) ⊥))))
⍝ ---- Bernoulli numbers from the tangent numbers T₁ … Tₘ (integers, Brent–Harvey / Knuth–Buckholtz):  Tₖ ← (k−1)!;  then for k = 2 … m,
⍝ j = k … m:  Tⱼ ← (j−k)·Tⱼ₋₁ + (j−k+2)·Tⱼ.   B₂ₘ = (−1)ᵐ⁻¹·2m·Tₘ / (4ᵐ(4ᵐ − 1)),  ζ(2m)/π²ᵐ = Tₘ / (2(4ᵐ − 1)(2m − 1)!).
fls_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔏 𝔇
fls_nt φ κ μ ≔ ((lt_nt κ μ) (∷ φ (fls_nt (⊠ᶻ φ (⊞ᶻ κ (◀ 1))) (⊞ᶻ κ (◀ 1)) μ)) ⊥)
tsc_nt ∶ 𝔏 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔏 𝔇
tsc_nt ρ π′ ι ≔ (ρ (θ τ ↦ ((η ↦ (∷ η (tsc_nt τ η (⊞ᶻ ι (◀ 1))))) (⊞ᶻ (⊠ᶻ ι π′) (⊠ᶻ (⊞ᶻ ι (◀ 1100)) θ)))) ⊥)
tg_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔏 𝔇 → 𝔇
tg_nt π′ ρ ≔ (ρ (θ τ ↦ ((ρ′ ↦ ((∅ (⌄ ρ′)) (hd ρ′) (tg_nt (hd ρ′) (⌄ ρ′)))) (tsc_nt ρ π′ ⊥))) π′)
⍝ the tangent number Tₘ (m ≥ 1)
tan_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇
tan_nt μ ≔ ((ρ ↦ (tg_nt (hd ρ) (⌄ ρ))) (fls_nt (◀ 1) ⊥ μ))
⍝ 4ᵐ
p4_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇
p4_nt μ ≔ ((∅ᶻ μ) (◀ 1) (⁴ᶻ (p4_nt (⊟ᶻ μ (◀ 1)))))
bernoulli ∶ ℕ → ℚ      ⍝ the Bernoulli number Bₙ, exactly, with B₁ = −1/2 (from the integer tangent numbers: O(n²) integer operations)
bernoulli ξ ≔ ((ν ↦ ((∅ᶻ ν) 1 ((eqz_nt ν (◀ 1)) (÷ 11101 1100) ((⌃ ν) 0 ((μ ↦ ((ϑ ↦ (⊜ (⊗ ((⌃ μ) (⊠ᶻ ν (tan_nt μ)) (⊖ᶻ (⊠ᶻ ν (tan_nt μ)))) (⊠ᶻ ϑ (⊟ᶻ ϑ (◀ 1)))))) (p4_nt μ))) (⊡ (½ᶻ ν))))))) (↓ᶻ ξ))
zetaeven ∶ ℕ → ℚ      ⍝ ζ(2n)/π²ⁿ, an exact rational (ζ(2) = π²/6, ζ(4) = π⁴/90, …; −1/2 for n = 0), from the tangent number Tₙ
zetaeven ξ ≔ ((μ ↦ ((∅ᶻ μ) (÷ 11101 1100) (⊜ (⊗ (tan_nt μ) (⊠ᶻ (◀ 1100) (⊠ᶻ (⊟ᶻ (p4_nt μ) (◀ 1)) (↓ᶻ (fact (up_nt (⊟ᶻ (⊞ᶻ μ μ) (◀ 1))))))))))) (↓ᶻ ξ))
⍝ ---- harmonic numbers over the common denominator L = lcm(1, …, n) = Π pᵉ (pᵉ ≤ n < pᵉ⁺¹)
mpw_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇
mpw_nt π′ ν ξ ≔ ((lt_nt ν (⊠ᶻ ξ π′)) ξ (mpw_nt π′ ν (⊠ᶻ ξ π′)))
lcn_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇
lcn_nt ν ≔ (foldl (ξ π′ ↦ (⊠ᶻ ξ (mpw_nt π′ ν π′))) (◀ 1) (prm_nt ν))
hsum_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇
hsum_nt λ κ ν ≔ ((lt_nt ν κ) ⊥ (⊞ᶻ (÷ᶻ λ κ) (hsum_nt λ (⊞ᶻ κ (◀ 1)) ν)))
harmonic ∶ ℕ → ℚ      ⍝ the harmonic number Hₙ = 1 + 1/2 + … + 1/n, exactly, in lowest terms (H₀ = 0)
harmonic ξ ≔ ((ν ↦ ((λ ↦ (⊜ (⊗ (hsum_nt λ (◀ 1) ν) λ))) (lcn_nt ν))) (↓ᶻ ξ))
⍝ ---- digits in a base, integer roots, perfect powers
dsm_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇
dsm_nt ν β ≔ ((∅ᶻ ν) ⊥ ((ψ ↦ (⊞ᶻ (▶ ψ) (dsm_nt (◀ ψ) β))) (⫽ᶻ ν β)))
digitsum ∶ ℤ → ℕ → ℕ      ⍝ the sum of the digits of |n| in base b ≥ 2 (base 1: |n|, base 0: 0)
digitsum ξ η ≔ ((ν β ↦ (up_nt ((lt_nt β (◀ 1100)) ((∅ᶻ β) ⊥ ν) (dsm_nt ν β)))) (absᶻ (↓ᶻ ξ)) (↓ᶻ η))
⍝ Newton from above for ⌊ν^(1/k)⌋:  x ← ((k−1)x + ⌊ν / xᵏ⁻¹⌋) div k  while it decreases;  start 2^(⌊(L+4)/2k⌋ + 1) > ν^(1/k)
irt′_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇
irt′_nt ν κ ξ ≔ ((η ↦ ((lt_nt η ξ) (irt′_nt ν κ η) ξ)) (dv_nt (⊞ᶻ (⊠ᶻ (⊟ᶻ κ (◀ 1)) ξ) (dv_nt ν (↓ᶻ (^ (up_nt ξ) (up_nt (⊟ᶻ κ (◀ 1))))))) κ))
irt_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇
irt_nt ν κ ≔ ((∅ᶻ κ) ⊥ ((∅ᶻ ν) ⊥ (irt′_nt ν κ (↓ᶻ (^ 1100 (up_nt (⊞ᶻ (dv_nt (⊞ᶻ (ul_nt (⊡ ν)) (◀ 111010000)) (⊞ᶻ κ κ)) (◀ 1))))))))
iroot ∶ ℕ → ℕ → ℕ      ⍝ ⌊n^(1/k)⌋, the integer k-th root (Newton's method from above); iroot(n, 0) = 0
iroot ξ η ≔ (up_nt (irt_nt (↓ᶻ ξ) (↓ᶻ η)))
⍝ ν = aᵖ for one of the primes p of the list (each p checked by its root)
ipw_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔏 𝔇 → 𝔹
ipw_nt ν ψ ≔ (∃ₗ (π′ ↦ (eqz_nt (↓ᶻ (^ (up_nt (irt_nt ν π′)) (up_nt π′))) ν)) ψ)
ispower ∶ ℤ → 𝔹      ⍝ n = aᵏ for an integer a and some k ≥ 2 (true for 0, 1, −1; a negative n needs an odd k); a k-th root test for every prime k ≤ log₂|n|
ispower ξ ≔ ((ν ↦ ((θ ↦ ((lt_nt θ (◀ 1100)) ⊤ (ipw_nt θ ((lt_nt ν ⊥) (⌄ (prm_nt (dv_nt (⊞ᶻ (ul_nt (⊡ θ)) (◀ 111010000)) (◀ 1100)))) (prm_nt (dv_nt (⊞ᶻ (ul_nt (⊡ θ)) (◀ 111010000)) (◀ 1100))))))) (absᶻ ν))) (↓ᶻ ξ))
⍝ ---- continued fractions
cf_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔏 𝔇
cf_nt π′ δ ≔ ((∅ᶻ δ) ⊥ ((ϑ ↦ (∷ ϑ (cf_nt δ (⊟ᶻ π′ (⊠ᶻ ϑ δ))))) (⌊ᶻ π′ δ)))
contfrac ∶ ℚ → 𝔏 ℤ      ⍝ the continued fraction [a₀; a₁, …, aₖ] of a rational (Euclid with floor quotients; aₖ ≥ 2 unless k = 0)
contfrac ξ ≔ ((θ ↦ (⫶ up_nt (cf_nt (◀ θ) (▶ θ)))) (⊜ ξ))
⍝ the fraction h/k with k made positive (0 when k = 0)
frc_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇 → ℚ
frc_nt η κ ≔ ((∅ᶻ κ) 0 ((lt_nt κ ⊥) (⊗ (⊡ (⊖ᶻ η)) (⊡ (⊖ᶻ κ))) (⊗ (⊡ η) (⊡ κ))))
cvp_nt ∶ 𝔏 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔏 (𝔓 𝔇 𝔇)
cvp_nt ξ η η′ κ κ′ ≔ (ξ (θ τ ↦ ((ϑ ϖ ↦ (∷ (⊗ ϑ ϖ) (cvp_nt τ ϑ η ϖ κ))) (⊞ᶻ (⊠ᶻ θ η) η′) (⊞ᶻ (⊠ᶻ θ κ) κ′))) ⊥)
convergents ∶ 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔏 ℚ      ⍝ the convergents hₖ/kₖ of [a₀; a₁, …] (hₖ = aₖhₖ₋₁ + hₖ₋₂, kₖ = aₖkₖ₋₁ + kₖ₋₂)
convergents ξ ≔ (⫶ (φ ↦ (frc_nt (◀ φ) (▶ φ))) (cvp_nt (⫶ ↓ᶻ ξ) (◀ 1) ⊥ ⊥ (◀ 1)))
⍝ √n = [a₀; period]:  m ← d·a − m,  d ← (n − m²)/d,  a ← ⌊(a₀ + m)/d⌋, until a = 2a₀
cfs_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔏 𝔇
cfs_nt ν ϑ μ δ ϖ ≔ ((μ′ ↦ ((δ′ ↦ ((ϖ′ ↦ (∷ ϖ′ ((eqz_nt ϖ′ (⊞ᶻ ϑ ϑ)) ⊥ (cfs_nt ν ϑ μ′ δ′ ϖ′)))) (dv_nt (⊞ᶻ ϑ μ′) δ′))) (⊡ (÷ᶻ (⊟ᶻ ν (⊠ᶻ μ′ μ′)) δ)))) (⊟ᶻ (⊠ᶻ δ ϖ) μ))
cfq_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔓 𝔇 (𝔏 𝔇)
cfq_nt ν ≔ ((ϑ ↦ (⊗ ϑ ((eqz_nt (⊠ᶻ ϑ ϑ) ν) ⊥ (cfs_nt ν ϑ ⊥ (◀ 1) ϑ)))) (√ᶻ ν))
cfsqrt ∶ ℕ → 𝔓 ℕ (𝔏 ℕ)      ⍝ √n = [a₀; a₁, …, aᵣ, a₁, …]: (a₀, the period a₁ … aᵣ); the period is empty when n is a square
cfsqrt ξ ≔ ((ψ ↦ (⊗ (up_nt (◀ ψ)) (⫶ up_nt (▶ ψ)))) (cfq_nt (↓ᶻ ξ)))
⍝ the fundamental solution is the convergent number r − 1 (r even) or 2r − 1 (r odd) of √D, r the length of the period
pell ∶ ℕ → 𝔓 ℕ ℕ      ⍝ the fundamental solution (x, y), y > 0 least, of x² − D·y² = 1, from the continued fraction of √D; (1, 0) when D is 0 or a square
pell ξ ≔ ((ψ ↦ ((∅ (▶ ψ)) (⊗ 1 0) ((φ ↦ (⊗ (up_nt (◀ φ)) (up_nt (▶ φ)))) (hd (drop′ ((odd_nt (▶ ψ)) (⊟ᶻ (⊞ᶻ (ul_nt (▶ ψ)) (ul_nt (▶ ψ))) (◀ 1)) (⊟ᶻ (ul_nt (▶ ψ)) (◀ 1))) (cvp_nt (∷ (◀ ψ) (⧺ (▶ ψ) (▶ ψ))) (◀ 1) ⊥ ⊥ (◀ 1))))))) (cfq_nt (↓ᶻ ξ)))
⍝ ---- Gaussian integers.  The prime 1 + i is the base up to a unit (b = i·(1 + i)), so its exponent in z is the number of trailing zero
⍝ digits.  The other Gaussian primes lie over the odd primes p | N(z): p itself when p ≡ 3 (mod 4), and π = gcd(p, t + i), π̄ when
⍝ p ≡ 1 (mod 4), t² ≡ −1 (t = z^((p−1)/4) for the least non-residue z).  Primes are normalised to Re > 0, Im ≥ 0 (⌜ᶻ) and listed by
⍝ norm, then by imaginary part; the unit is z divided by the product of the prime powers.
tz_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔓 (𝔏 𝔹) 𝔇
tz_nt ξ υ ≔ ((⌃ ξ) (⊗ υ ξ) (tz_nt (⌄ ξ) (∷ ⊤ υ)))
nz_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇
nz_nt ζ ≔ (⊠ᶻ ζ (∗ᶻ ζ))
pwz_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇
pwz_nt ζ ν ≔ (↓ᶻ (^ (up_nt ζ) (up_nt ν)))
gpi_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇
gpi_nt π′ ≔ (ggcdᶻ π′ (⊞ᶻ (pmd_nt π′ (qnr_nt π′ (◀ 1100)) (dv_nt (⊟ᶻ π′ (◀ 1)) (◀ 111010000))) (◀ 11)))
⍝ how often π divides ζ: (count, rest)
dvg_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔓 𝔇 𝔇
dvg_nt ζ π′ κ ≔ ((∅ᶻ (remᶻ ζ π′)) (dvg_nt (⊡ (÷ᶻ ζ π′)) π′ (⊞ᶻ κ (◀ 1))) (⊗ κ ζ))
gent_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔓 𝔇 𝔇 → 𝔏 (𝔓 𝔇 𝔇)
gent_nt π′ ψ ≔ ((∅ᶻ (◀ ψ)) ⊥ (∷ (⊗ π′ (◀ ψ)) ⊥))
⍝ the Gaussian prime powers over the rational primes of the list (the factorisation of N(ζ), ζ odd)
gpe_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔏 (𝔓 𝔇 𝔇) → 𝔏 (𝔓 𝔇 𝔇)
gpe_nt ζ φ′ ≔ (φ′ (φ τ ↦ ((m3_nt (◀ φ)) ((ψ ↦ (∷ (⊗ (◀ φ) (◀ ψ)) (gpe_nt (▶ ψ) τ))) (dvg_nt ζ (◀ φ) ⊥)) ((ϑ ↦ ((ϖ ↦ ((ψ ↦ ((ψ′ ↦ (⧺ (gent_nt ϑ ψ) (⧺ (gent_nt ϖ ψ′) (gpe_nt (▶ ψ′) τ)))) (dvg_nt (▶ ψ) ϖ ⊥))) (dvg_nt ζ ϑ ⊥))) (⌜ᶻ (∗ᶻ ϑ)))) (gpi_nt (◀ φ))))) ⊥)
⍝ Gaussian order: by norm, then by imaginary part
gcmp_nt ∶ 𝔓 𝔇 α → 𝔓 𝔇 α → 𝔹
gcmp_nt φ φ′ ≔ ((⋚ʳ (⊟ᶻ (nz_nt (◀ φ)) (nz_nt (◀ φ′)))) ⊤ (lt_nt (ℑᶻ (◀ φ)) (ℑᶻ (◀ φ′))) ⊥)
gfa_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔓 𝔇 (𝔏 (𝔓 𝔇 𝔇))
gfa_nt ζ ≔ ((ψ ↦ ((ρ ↦ (⊗ (⊡ (÷ᶻ ζ (foldl (ξ φ ↦ (⊠ᶻ ξ (pwz_nt (◀ φ) (▶ φ)))) (◀ 1) ρ))) ρ)) (msort_nt gcmp_nt (⧺ ((∅ (◀ ψ)) ⊥ (∷ (⊗ (◀ 1110) (ul_nt (◀ ψ))) ⊥)) (gpe_nt (▶ ψ) (fct_nt (nz_nt (▶ ψ)))))))) (tz_nt ζ ⊥))
gaussfactor ∶ ℤ[i] → 𝔓 ℤ[i] (𝔏 (𝔓 ℤ[i] ℕ))      ⍝ z = u·Π πᵉ: (the unit u, the list of (π, e)), π Gaussian primes with Re > 0, Im ≥ 0, by norm then imaginary part; (0, []) for 0. Through the factorisation of N(z) and Gaussian gcds; 1 + i from the trailing zero digits
gaussfactor ξ ≔ ((ζ ↦ ((∅ᶻ ζ) (⊗ 0 ⊥) ((ψ ↦ (⊗ (up_nt (◀ ψ)) (⫶ (φ ↦ (⊗ (up_nt (◀ φ)) (up_nt (▶ φ)))) (▶ ψ)))) (gfa_nt ζ)))) (↓ᶻ ξ))
⍝ a real p is a Gaussian prime when p is a prime ≡ 3 (mod 4)
gp3_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔹
gp3_nt ν ≔ (∧ (m3_nt ν) (ispr_nt ν))
igp_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔹
igp_nt ζ ≔ ((ϑ ϖ ↦ ((∅ᶻ ϖ) (gp3_nt (absᶻ ϑ)) ((∅ᶻ ϑ) (gp3_nt (absᶻ ϖ)) (ispr_nt (⊞ᶻ (⊠ᶻ ϑ ϑ) (⊠ᶻ ϖ ϖ)))))) (ℜᶻ ζ) (ℑᶻ ζ))
isgaussprime ∶ ℤ[i] → 𝔹      ⍝ z is a Gaussian prime: N(z) a prime when Re z·Im z ≠ 0, else |Re z| or |Im z| a prime ≡ 3 (mod 4)
isgaussprime ξ ≔ (igp_nt (↓ᶻ ξ))
⍝ ---- sums of two squares: the Gaussian integers of norm n, up to units, are (1+i)ˢ · Π qᶠ · Π πʲπ̄ᵉ⁻ʲ (j = 0 … e) — none when a prime
⍝ q ≡ 3 (mod 4) has an odd exponent.  Each z = x + iy gives (max(|x|,|y|), min(|x|,|y|)); the pairs are sorted by b and repeated ones dropped.
s2c_nt ∶ 𝔏 𝔇 → 𝔓 𝔇 𝔇 → 𝔏 𝔇
s2c_nt ζ′ φ ≔ ((eqz_nt (◀ φ) (◀ 1100)) ((ϑ ↦ (⫶ (ζ ↦ (⊠ᶻ ζ ϑ)) ζ′)) (pwz_nt (◀ 1110) (▶ φ))) ((m3_nt (◀ φ)) ((ϑ ↦ (⫶ (ζ ↦ (⊠ᶻ ζ ϑ)) ζ′)) (pwz_nt (◀ φ) (½ᶻ (▶ φ)))) ((ϑ ↦ ((ϖ ↦ (concat (⫶ (ι ↦ ((χ ↦ (⫶ (ζ ↦ (⊠ᶻ ζ χ)) ζ′)) (⊠ᶻ (pwz_nt ϑ ι) (pwz_nt ϖ (⊟ᶻ (▶ φ) ι))))) (upl_nt ⊥ (▶ φ))))) (⌜ᶻ (∗ᶻ ϑ)))) (gpi_nt (◀ φ)))))
⍝ 0, 1, …, ν as digits
upl_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔏 𝔇
upl_nt ξ ν ≔ ((lt_nt ν ξ) ⊥ (∷ ξ (upl_nt (⊞ᶻ ξ (◀ 1)) ν)))
s2p_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔓 𝔇 𝔇
s2p_nt ζ ≔ ((ϑ ϖ ↦ ((lt_nt ϑ ϖ) (⊗ ϖ ϑ) (⊗ ϑ ϖ))) (absᶻ (ℜᶻ ζ)) (absᶻ (ℑᶻ ζ)))
s2s_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔏 (𝔓 𝔇 𝔇)
s2s_nt ν ≔ ((lt_nt ν ⊥) ⊥ ((∅ᶻ ν) (∷ (⊗ ⊥ ⊥) ⊥) ((ψ ↦ ((∃ₗ (φ ↦ (∧ (m3_nt (◀ φ)) (⌃ (▶ φ)))) ψ) ⊥ (ddp_nt ▶ (msort_nt (φ φ′ ↦ (lt_nt (▶ φ) (▶ φ′))) (⫶ s2p_nt (foldl s2c_nt (∷ (◀ 1) ⊥) ψ)))))) (fct_nt ν))))
sumtwosquares ∶ ℤ → 𝔏 (𝔓 ℕ ℕ)      ⍝ every way to write n = a² + b² with a ≥ b ≥ 0, by increasing b; from the Gaussian factorisation of n ([] when n < 0 or a prime ≡ 3 mod 4 divides n to an odd power)
sumtwosquares ξ ≔ (⫶ (φ ↦ (⊗ (up_nt (◀ φ)) (up_nt (▶ φ)))) (s2s_nt (↓ᶻ ξ)))
⍝ the Gaussian primes of norm ≤ n: 1 + i, π and π̄ over p ≡ 1 (mod 4), p ≤ n, and q ≡ 3 (mod 4) with q² ≤ n
gps_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔏 𝔇
gps_nt ν π′ ≔ ((eqz_nt π′ (◀ 1100)) (∷ (◀ 1110) ⊥) ((m3_nt π′) ((lt_nt ν (⊠ᶻ π′ π′)) ⊥ (∷ π′ ⊥)) ((ϑ ↦ (∷ ϑ (∷ (⌜ᶻ (∗ᶻ ϑ)) ⊥))) (gpi_nt π′))))
gaussprimes ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℤ[i]      ⍝ the Gaussian primes of norm ≤ n (normalised: Re > 0, Im ≥ 0), by norm then imaginary part
gaussprimes ξ ≔ ((ν ↦ (⫶ (φ ↦ (up_nt (◀ φ))) (msort_nt gcmp_nt (⫶ (ζ ↦ (⊗ ζ ⊥)) (concat (⫶ (gps_nt ν) (prm_nt ν))))))) (↓ᶻ ξ))
⍝ ---- more: gcd and lcm of lists, squares, prime powers, coprimality, totatives, primitive roots, Ramanujan sums, Wilson's test
gcdlist ∶ 𝔏 ℤ → ℕ      ⍝ the gcd of a list of integers (0 for the empty list); of Gaussian integers, normalised to Re > 0, Im ≥ 0
gcdlist ∶ 𝔏 ℤ[i] → ℤ[i]
gcdlist ξ ≔ (foldl gcd 0 ξ)
lcl_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇
lcl_nt ξ η ≔ ((∨ (∅ᶻ ξ) (∅ᶻ η)) ⊥ (⊡ (÷ᶻ (absᶻ (⊠ᶻ ξ η)) (gcdᶻ ξ η))))
lcmlist ∶ 𝔏 ℤ → ℕ      ⍝ the least common multiple of a list of integers (1 for the empty list, 0 when an element is 0)
lcmlist ξ ≔ (up_nt (foldl (η ζ ↦ (lcl_nt η (↓ᶻ ζ))) (◀ 1) ξ))
issquare ∶ ℤ → 𝔹      ⍝ n is a perfect square (false for n < 0; through the integer square root)
issquare ξ ≔ (issq_nt (↓ᶻ ξ))
isprimepower ∶ ℤ → 𝔹      ⍝ n = pᵏ for a prime p and k ≥ 1 (n > 0; from the factorisation)
isprimepower ξ ≔ (∧ (≻ ξ 0) ((θ ↦ (∧ (¬ (∅ θ)) (∅ (⌄ θ)))) (fcq_nt ξ)))
iscoprime ∶ ℤ → ℤ → 𝔹      ⍝ gcd(a, b) = 1; for Gaussian integers: the gcd is a unit
iscoprime ∶ ℤ[i] → ℤ[i] → 𝔹
iscoprime ξ η ≔ (≐ (gcd ξ η) 1)
totatives ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ      ⍝ the k in 1 … n with gcd(k, n) = 1, ascending (φ(n) of them; [] for n = 0)
totatives ξ ≔ (filter (κ ↦ (≐ (gcd κ ξ) 1)) (upto 1 ξ))
⍝ gᵏ mod ν for κ ≤ k ≤ φ with gcd(k, φ) = 1  (ξ = gᵏ)
prl_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔏 𝔇
prl_nt ν φ γ κ ξ ≔ ((lt_nt φ κ) ⊥ ((ψ ↦ ((eqz_nt (gcdᶻ κ φ) (◀ 1)) (∷ ξ ψ) ψ)) (prl_nt ν φ γ (⊞ᶻ κ (◀ 1)) (mod_nt (⊠ᶻ ξ γ) ν))))
primitiveroots ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ      ⍝ all primitive roots modulo n, ascending: gᵏ mod n for the k ≤ φ(n) prime to φ(n), g = primroot(n); [] when there is none (O(n) products)
primitiveroots ξ ≔ ((ν γ ↦ ((∅ᶻ γ) ⊥ (⫶ up_nt (msort_nt lt_nt (prl_nt ν (↓ᶻ (totient ξ)) γ (◀ 1) γ))))) (↓ᶻ ξ) (↓ᶻ (primroot ξ)))
ramanujansum ∶ ℕ → ℤ → ℤ      ⍝ Ramanujan's sum c_q(n) = Σ μ(q/d)·d over the divisors d of gcd(q, n): the sum of the n-th powers of the primitive q-th roots of unity (c₀(n) = 0)
ramanujansum κ ξ ≔ ((≐ κ 0) 0 (sumof (⫶ (δ ↦ (⊠ (mobius (÷ κ δ)) δ)) (divisors (gcd κ ξ)))))
⍝ the product κ·(κ − 1)·…·2·φ modulo ν
wil_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇
wil_nt ν κ φ ≔ ((lt_nt κ (◀ 1100)) φ (wil_nt ν (⊟ᶻ κ (◀ 1)) (mod_nt (⊠ᶻ φ κ) ν)))
wilson ∶ ℤ → 𝔹      ⍝ Wilson's theorem as a primality test: n ≥ 2 and (n − 1)! ≡ −1 (mod n), true exactly for the primes (O(n) modular products: a demonstration, not a fast test)
wilson ξ ≔ ((ν ↦ (∧ (lt_nt (◀ 1) ν) (eqz_nt (wil_nt ν (⊟ᶻ ν (◀ 1)) (◀ 1)) (⊟ᶻ ν (◀ 1))))) (↓ᶻ ξ))
⍝ ---- more Gaussian integers: the Gaussian primes of a given norm, the next Gaussian prime, perfect powers in ℤ[i]
⍝ the Gaussian primes of norm μ (normalised), by imaginary part: 1 + i for 2; π, π̄ for a prime ≡ 1 (mod 4); q for μ = q², q ≡ 3 (mod 4)
gpm_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔏 𝔇
gpm_nt μ ≔ ((eqz_nt μ (◀ 1100)) (∷ (◀ 1110) ⊥) ((ispr_nt μ) ((m3_nt μ) ⊥ ((ϑ ↦ ((ϖ ↦ ((lt_nt (ℑᶻ ϑ) (ℑᶻ ϖ)) (∷ ϑ (∷ ϖ ⊥)) (∷ ϖ (∷ ϑ ⊥)))) (⌜ᶻ (∗ᶻ ϑ)))) (gpi_nt μ))) ((ρ ↦ ((∧ (eqz_nt (⊠ᶻ ρ ρ) μ) (gp3_nt ρ)) (∷ ρ ⊥) ⊥)) (√ᶻ μ))))
⍝ the first Gaussian prime of norm ≥ μ, after imaginary part ι when ς (at the norm μ itself)
ngp_nt ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔹 → 𝔇
ngp_nt μ ι ς ≔ ((ψ ↦ ((∅ ψ) (ngp_nt (⊞ᶻ μ (◀ 1)) ι ⊥) (hd ψ))) (filter (ζ ↦ (∨ (¬ ς) (lt_nt ι (ℑᶻ ζ)))) (gpm_nt μ)))
nextgaussprime ∶ ℤ[i] → ℤ[i]      ⍝ the next Gaussian prime after z in the order of gaussprimes: the normalised (Re > 0, Im ≥ 0) π with (N(π), Im π) > (N(z), Im z) least
nextgaussprime ξ ≔ ((ζ ↦ (up_nt (ngp_nt (nz_nt ζ) (ℑᶻ ζ) ⊤))) (↓ᶻ ξ))
isgausspower ∶ ℤ[i] → 𝔹      ⍝ z = wᵏ for a Gaussian integer w and some k ≥ 2 (true for 0 and the units): with z = u·Π πᵉ, g = gcd of the e has an odd prime factor, or g is even and u = ±1
isgausspower ξ ≔ ((ζ ↦ ((∅ᶻ ζ) ⊤ ((ψ ↦ ((γ ↦ ((∅ᶻ γ) ⊤ ((θ ↦ ((∃ₗ (φ ↦ (¬ (eqz_nt (◀ φ) (◀ 1100)))) θ) ⊤ (∧ (¬ (∅ θ)) (realᶻ (◀ ψ))))) (fct_nt γ)))) (foldl (η φ ↦ (gcdᶻ η (▶ φ))) ⊥ (▶ ψ)))) (gfa_nt ζ)))) (↓ᶻ ξ))
